.TH QCSTATS 1 "2026-10-25" "qcstats" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
qcstats \- telemetry sampler for the Arduino Ventuno Q
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B qcstats
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ interval_ms ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B qcstats
samples the hardware telemetry of an Arduino Ventuno Q (Qualcomm QCS8275 /
Dragonwing IQ\-8275) and prints one sample per line: per\-core CPU utilisation and
per\-cluster frequency for all three frequency policies, memory in use, GPU
frequency, thermal zone temperatures, board input power, fan duty and rpm, and the
kernel's LMh throttle counters.
.PP
It reads only paths that exist on that board, and it writes nothing to the system \-
with one opt\-in exception, see
.B \-\-gpu\-busy
below. It needs no privileges: CPU frequency comes from
.IR scaling_cur_freq ,
not from the root\-only
.IR cpuinfo_cur_freq .
.PP
Nothing is printed for the first interval. CPU percentages are a delta and need two
.I /proc/stat
readings, so there is nothing truthful to print before one interval has passed.
.PP
A source that cannot be read is reported as
.BR absent ,
never as a zero:
.B n/a
in the plain format,
.B null
in JSON, and an empty field in CSV. A zero means a measurement was taken and it was
zero \-
.I 0 rpm
is a fan that is off, and
.I 0%
is an idle core.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-plain
One compact line per sample, for reading. The default.
.TP
.B \-\-json
One JSON object per sample, newline\-delimited (NDJSON), preceded by one
.I meta
line naming the kernel and image the run saw. The field\-by\-field contract is
versioned; see
.BR "JSON SCHEMA" .
.TP
.B \-\-csv
CSV with a header row. An empty field is an absent source.
.TP
.BI \-\-count " N"
Emit
.I N
samples and exit. The default, 0, runs until killed. Note that
.B \-\-count 1
still costs one interval, for the reason given above.
.TP
.BI \-\-interval " MS"
Sampling interval in milliseconds. Default 1000, floor 50; a smaller value is
clamped to the floor. The positional
.I interval_ms
argument does the same thing.
.TP
.BI \-\-zones " LIST"
Comma\-separated thermal zones, by the short printed name
.RI ( cpuss-0-0 )
or the full type
.RI ( cpuss-0-0-thermal ).
Default: five zones.
.TP
.B \-\-all\-zones
Every thermal zone the kernel exposes, in index order \- 48 on this board. Mutually
exclusive with
.BR \-\-zones .
.TP
.B \-\-npu
Report Hexagon NSP utilisation and clock over FastRPC. Needs
.I libcdsprpc.so.1
and access to the FastRPC device; the library is resolved at run time and reported as
absent when it is missing. Polled at 1 Hz regardless of
.BR \-\-interval ,
because one query costs about 1.12 ms and loads the DSP itself.
.TP
.B \-\-gpu\-busy
Report the true GPU busy percentage.
.B Needs root, and is the one thing qcstats writes:
it enables the
.I devfreq_monitor
tracepoint, in a trace instance of its own so that any tracing already in use is
undisturbed, and removes it again on exit.
.B SIGINT,
.B SIGTERM
and
.B SIGHUP
are handled so that an interrupted run still restores it;
.B SIGKILL
is the one signal that leaves the instance and the enabled event behind, and removing
the instance directory undoes it.
.IP
An idle GPU is runtime\-suspended and its devfreq governor stops polling, so the
tracepoint is silent and 0 is then reported from the GPU's
.IR runtime_status :
a powered\-down GPU is executing nothing. A GPU that is awake but has not yet
completed a polling window is reported as absent rather than as a stale value.
.TP
.BI \-\-logfile " P"
Write samples to
.I P
instead of standard output; notices still go to standard error.
.B This truncates P,
so that a CSV header cannot land in the middle of a file.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print usage to standard output and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the sampler version and the JSON schema version, one per line, and exit.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success, including a run in which sources were absent.
.TP
.B 2
Usage error, or a
.B \-\-logfile
that could not be opened.
.PP
Nothing in the sampling loop changes the exit status: a board with no fan and no power
sensor still exits 0. Absence is a reading, not a failure.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B QCSTATS_SYSROOT
Read sysfs and procfs under this directory instead of
.IR / ,
so the sampler can be exercised against a captured tree off\-hardware. It relocates
reads only; the
.B \-\-gpu\-busy
tracepoint path is absolute and is not relocated.
.SH JSON SCHEMA
.B \-\-json
output carries a schema version
.RI ( "\"v\":1" )
that is independent of the program version: a field is never renamed or retyped
without it changing. The per\-field contract is in
.I docs/json\-schema\-v1.md
in the source distribution.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B qcstats
One line per second until interrupted.
.TP
.B qcstats --json --count 5
Five NDJSON samples, then exit.
.TP
.B qcstats --csv --interval 500 --logfile run.csv
Two samples a second to a CSV file.
.TP
.B qcstats --all-zones --count 1
Every thermal zone, once.
.SH BUGS
It targets one board. On other hardware the paths it reads are simply absent, and are
reported as absent; what differently\-shaped paths would produce is untested.
.SH AUTHOR
Hans Kramer.
